-- title:
--   The executable color evaluator returns the prescribed two-bit color
-- statement:
--   Let $W,m,u,d$ be natural numbers with $m<2^W$. A coloring parameter consists of two coordinates $a,b<W$ and a map $\phi:\{0,1\}^2\to\{0,1,2\}$. Suppose a program contains the specified color-evaluation body and the recursive mask-erasing body. Memory $\mu$ stores $2^j$ at $u+j$ for $j\le W$. For space, word, and depth limits $S,M,D$, assume
--   $$S\le M,\qquad u+W+1\le S,\qquad2^{W+1}\le M,\qquad d+W+1\le D.$$
--   The call with $W,m,a,b$, the four values of $\phi$, and $u$ succeeds within $200W+210$ steps and returns
--   $$r=\phi\bigl(\operatorname{bit}_a(m),\operatorname{bit}_b(m)\bigr),\qquad\mu'=\mu.$$
--
--   This certifies direct evaluation of one member of the deterministic coloring family on an original input index.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightColorIndex.lean#L44-L108

